.SH "Enumeration Type Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "enum \fBt_token_type\fP"

.PP
Token types for the shell's lexer\&. These types represent the different kinds of tokens that can be identified in the shell's input\&. They include words, operators, and special tokens like EOF and errors\&. 
.PP
\fBEnumerator\fP
.in +1c
.TP
\f(BITOK_WORD \fP
A word token ex: "ls" or "echo" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_PIPE \fP
A pipe token ex: "|" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_AND \fP
A logical AND token ex: "&&" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_OR \fP
A logical OR token ex: "||" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_SEMICOLON \fP
A semicolon token ex: ";" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_AMPERSAND \fP
An ampersand token ex: "&" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_NEWLINE \fP
A newline token (end of command) 
.TP
\f(BITOK_REDIR_IN \fP
A redirect input token ex: "<" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_REDIR_OUT \fP
A redirect output token ex: ">" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_REDIR_APPEND \fP
A redirect append token ex: ">>" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_HEREDOC \fP
A heredoc token ex: "<<" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_REDIR_DUP_IN \fP
A duplicate redirect input token ex: "<&" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_REDIR_DUP_OUT \fP
A duplicate redirect output token ex: ">&" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_LPAREN \fP
A left parenthesis token ex: "(" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_RPAREN \fP
A right parenthesis token ex: ")" 
.TP
\f(BITOK_EOF \fP
An end-of-file token 
.TP
\f(BITOK_ERROR \fP
An error token (invalid syntax) 
.SH "Function Documentation"
.PP 
.SS "int is_operator (char c)"

.PP
check if a char is the beginning of an operator 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIc\fP character to check
.RE
.PP
check if the character is in "&|><;{}\\n" 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
0 | 1 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int is_operator_start (const char * line)"

.PP
check if a string is an operator 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIline\fP string of operator to test
.RE
.PP
manage the digits in case of redirection then call is_operator 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 | 0 
.RE
.PP

.SS "int lexer_check_quotes (const char * input, char * unclosed_quote)"

.PP
Check for unclosed quotes\&. Sets *unclosed_quote to the quote char ('\\'', '"') or 0 if balanced\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP The input string to check\&. 
.br
\fIunclosed_quote\fP A pointer to a char where the unclosed quote will be stored\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
1 if an open quote is found, 0 if balanced\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "void lexer_free_tokens (t_list * tokens)"

.PP
Free an entire token list (tokens + strings + nodes)\&. This function frees all memory associated with a list of tokens\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItokens\fP The list of tokens to free\&. 
.RE
.PP

.SS "t_list * lexer_tokenize (const char * input)"

.PP
Tokenize an input string into a list of tokens\&. This function takes a string as input and breaks it down into individual tokens based on the shell's syntax rules\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP The input string to tokenize\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A pointer to a t_list containing the parsed tokens, or NULL on error\&.
.RE
.PP
Tokenize an input string into a list of tokens\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIinput\fP The string input from readline
.RE
.PP
skip spaces and recognize the type of token before adding it in the list\&. The memory is allocated and the list must be freed\&. 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
t_list* with t_token* as content 
.RE
.PP

.SS "t_list * read_operator (const char ** line)"

.PP
read the operator and tokenize it 
.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fIthe\fP string of the operator
.RE
.PP
choose the good function to tokenize 
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
a t_list* node 
.RE
.PP

.SS "t_list * token_new (\fBt_token_type\fP type, char * value, int io_number)"

.PP
Token helpers (used by lexer internally and by tests) These functions are used to create and free tokens, check for operators, and read operators and words from the input string\&. They are also used by the unit tests to verify the correctness of the lexer implementation\&.

.PP
\fBParameters\fP
.RS 4
\fItype\fP The type of the token to create\&. 
.br
\fIvalue\fP The raw string value of the token (with quotes preserved)\&. 
.br
\fIio_number\fP The file descriptor number for redirection tokens (set to -1 if not applicable)\&.
.RE
.PP
\fBReturns\fP
.RS 4
A new t_list node containing the created token, or NULL on allocation failure\&. 
.RE
.PP

